    "# STABILIS — Customer Purchase Propensity Modeling\n",
    "\n",
    "## Stage 2: Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "Objective:\n",
    "Predict whether a customer will make a purchase during a future observation period using only information available before the prediction period."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9a12f3c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.1 Define the ML Business Problem\n",
    "\n",
    "Business Question:\n",
    "Which customers are likely to make a purchase in a future period?\n",
    "\n",
    "Target:\n",
    "PurchaseInFuture\n",
    "\n",
    "1 = customer makes at least one future purchase\n",
    "0 = customer makes no future purchase\n",
    "\n",
    "The final PurchaseProbability will be generated from the trained ML model's predict_proba() output."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "5de2edcc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Rows: 410763\n",
      "Minimum date: 2019-12-01 07:45:00\n",
      "Maximum date: 2020-12-09 20:01:00\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_excel(\"../Data/Customers_Transactions.xlsx\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df[\"EventDateTime\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"EventDateTime\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove exact duplicate rows identified during Stage 1\n",
    "df = df.drop_duplicates().copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Rows:\", len(df))\n",
    "print(\"Minimum date:\", df[\"EventDateTime\"].min())\n",
    "print(\"Maximum date:\", df[\"EventDateTime\"].max())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "92a791e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.2 Temporal Prediction Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "The prediction cutoff is defined as 90 days before the final transaction date.\n",
    "\n",
    "Customer features will be calculated using transactions available on or before the cutoff.\n",
    "\n",
    "The target variable, PurchaseInFuture, indicates whether the customer makes at least one purchase during the following 90-day period."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "11f3b496",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Maximum date: 2020-12-09 20:01:00\n",
      "Prediction cutoff: 2020-09-10 20:01:00\n",
      "Future window ends: 2020-12-09 20:01:00\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Define prediction cutoff\n",
    "max_date = df[\"EventDateTime\"].max()\n",
    "\n",
    "cutoff_date = max_date - pd.Timedelta(days=90)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Maximum date:\", max_date)\n",
    "print(\"Prediction cutoff:\", cutoff_date)\n",
    "print(\"Future window ends:\", max_date)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "ad31263f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Historical rows: 260364\n",
      "Future rows: 150399\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Historical period: information available for feature creation\n",
    "historical_df = df[\n",
    "    df[\"EventDateTime\"] <= cutoff_date\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Future period: used only to create the prediction target\n",
    "future_df = df[\n",
    "    (df[\"EventDateTime\"] > cutoff_date) &\n",
    "    (df[\"EventDateTime\"] <= max_date)\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Historical rows:\", len(historical_df))\n",
    "print(\"Future rows:\", len(future_df))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "3d9acaa2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Customers with future purchases: 2877\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "future_purchases = (\n",
    "    future_df[future_df[\"EventType\"] == \"Purchased\"]\n",
    "    .groupby(\"UserID\")\n",
    "    .size()\n",
    "    .rename(\"FuturePurchaseCount\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Customers with future purchases:\", len(future_purchases))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "49e485cd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "PurchaseInFuture\n",
      "1    1956\n",
      "0    1493\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Customers present in the historical period\n",
    "customer_base = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"UserID\": historical_df[\"UserID\"].unique()\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "customer_base = customer_base.merge(\n",
    "    future_purchases,\n",
    "    on=\"UserID\",\n",
    "    how=\"left\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "customer_base[\"FuturePurchaseCount\"] = (\n",
    "    customer_base[\"FuturePurchaseCount\"]\n",
    "    .fillna(0)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "customer_base[\"PurchaseInFuture\"] = (\n",
    "    customer_base[\"FuturePurchaseCount\"] > 0\n",
    ").astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(customer_base[\"PurchaseInFuture\"].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0c500a88",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2.3 Historical Customer Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Customer features are calculated using only transactions available on or before the prediction cutoff.\n",
    "\n",
    "Features include purchase frequency, gross revenue, average basket value, recency, product breadth, and return behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "No information from the future prediction window is used in feature creation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "556ed21f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create line value from transaction-level data\n",
    "historical_df[\"LineValue\"] = (\n",
    "    historical_df[\"Quantity\"] * historical_df[\"UnitPrice\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Separate purchases and returns\n",
    "historical_purchases = historical_df[\n",
    "    historical_df[\"EventType\"] == \"Purchased\"\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "historical_returns = historical_df[\n",
    "    historical_df[\"EventType\"] == \"Returned\"\n",
    "].copy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "3a3e04b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "purchase_features = (\n",
    "    historical_purchases\n",
    "    .groupby(\"UserID\")\n",
    "    .agg(\n",
    "        PurchaseFrequency=(\"EventID\", \"nunique\"),\n",
    "        GrossRevenue=(\"LineValue\", \"sum\"),\n",
    "        UniqueProducts=(\"ProductID\", \"nunique\"),\n",
    "        LastPurchaseDate=(\"EventDateTime\", \"max\")\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    .reset_index()\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "purchase_features[\"AverageBasketValue\"] = (\n",
    "    purchase_features[\"GrossRevenue\"]\n",
    "    / purchase_features[\"PurchaseFrequency\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "purchase_features[\"RecencyDays\"] = (\n",
    "    cutoff_date - purchase_features[\"LastPurchaseDate\"]\n",
    ").dt.total_seconds() / (24 * 60 * 60)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "386e654f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "return_features = (\n",
    "    historical_returns\n",
    "    .groupby(\"UserID\")\n",
    "    .agg(\n",
    "        ReturnEvents=(\"EventID\", \"nunique\"),\n",
    "        ReturnValue=(\"LineValue\", lambda x: x.abs().sum())\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    .reset_index()\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "1c364e37",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model_df = customer_base.merge(\n",
    "    purchase_features,\n",
    "    on=\"UserID\",\n",
    "    how=\"left\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_df = model_df.merge(\n",
    "    return_features,\n",
    "    on=\"UserID\",\n",
    "    how=\"left\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_df[\"ReturnEvents\"] = model_df[\"ReturnEvents\"].fillna(0)\n",
    "model_df[\"ReturnValue\"] = model_df[\"ReturnValue\"].fillna(0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 11,
   "id": "b7997957",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model_df[\"ReturnValueRate\"] = np.where(\n",
    "    model_df[\"GrossRevenue\"] > 0,\n",
    "    model_df[\"ReturnValue\"] / model_df[\"GrossRevenue\"],\n",
    "    0\n",
    ")"
   ]
